course: dictionary
lesson: 1856
title: Words from history: codex
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A codex is an old book written by hand, with its pages fastened together. Look for the clue words in the sentence around it. «After the conquest, Nahua writers working with the Spanish friar Bernardino de Sahagún recorded Aztec memories of the conquest in the Florentine Codex.» Recorded, written and memories tell you that a codex is a book where people wrote down what they remembered.
explain: The sentence «They studied an ancient codex in the museum» gives another clue. Ancient means very old, so a codex can be a very old book. Test your meaning by swapping it in: "They studied a very old hand-written book in the museum" still makes sense, so you are right.
explain: Codex has an older meaning too: a book of laws or rules. Context tells you which meaning fits. If the sentence is about writing history, it means a hand-written book. If it is about what citizens must obey, it means a book of rules.
fact: «Codex» means an old book written by hand, with its pages bound together.
fact: The plural of codex can be codices or codexes.
fact: A codex replaced the scroll because it was easier to use.
fact: «Codex Sinaiticus» is an early Bible, written by hand in very old times.
fact: The Dresden Codex is an ancient Mayan book, and the Florentine Codex records Aztec memories.
exercise: «In history lessons we study the Dresden Codex, an ancient Mayan book.» What is a codex? | A rolled-up piece of paper for letters | A type of stone carving | A map of the stars | *An old book written by hand, with its pages bound together
exercise: Why did the codex replace the scroll? | *Because it was easier to use | Because it could only be read in the dark | Because it was made of gold | Because scrolls were heavier than stones
exercise: «The king's codex told every citizen what was allowed.» What does codex mean here? | A painting of a king | An old hand-written history | A story for children | *A book of laws or rules
test:  «The monks copied the ancient codex by hand, page by page.» What does ancient mean here? | Very loud | Brand new | Hidden | Very small | *Very old
test:  Which of these is an early Bible? | Dresden Codex | Florentine Codex | *Codex Sinaiticus | Leonardo's sketchbook
exam: «The codex was a book of rules that every village had to follow.» Which meaning of codex fits best? | A small sketch by an artist | A hand-written history of the Aztecs | *A book of laws or rules | A type of rolled scroll
